# LLM Cost Telemetry -- Universal Observability

Every LLM call this platform makes MUST be counted, costed, attributed
to a tenant and a patient where applicable, and surfaced in the
existing dashboard cost trackers without UI changes.

The contract is owned by:

- DI-LEO-AI-506 -- universal LLM token + cost telemetry (async helper)
- DI-LEO-AI-515 -- sync entry-point telemetry (`LLMClient.converse`,
  `invoke_with_fallback`)
- DO-LEO-AI-506 / DO-LEO-AI-514 -- recorder + invoke_llm_json + sync
  `converse` / fallback plumbing + finalise writes
- R-LEO-AI-506  -- under-billing risk if pipelines skip the contract
- VT-LEO-AI-508 -- verification of the async helper (token extraction,
  recorder isolation, Assessment + AuditEvent writes, telemetry-
  failure isolation)
- VT-LEO-AI-513 -- verification of the sync entry points
  (`LLMClient.converse` + `invoke_with_fallback` callback parity,
  failure-path emission, callback-exception isolation, recorder
  pickup of sync calls)

The wire format is fixed by DI-LEO-AI-068 (per-tenant billing) and the
existing `LLMSpendPanel` / `AuditTrailTab` components. Do not invent
new shapes.

---

## 1. Every LLM Call MUST Go Through a Sanctioned Entry Point

There are exactly THREE sanctioned LLM entry points in this codebase.
Each of them already wires `track_llm_usage` so the cost telemetry
contract is satisfied automatically. Use one of these:

| Entry point                                              | When to use                                                  | Async? |
|----------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|--------|
| `libs.llm_client.json_helper.invoke_llm_json`            | Async features that want a JSON response with retry          | Async  |
| `libs.llm_client.factory.create_llm(...).converse(...)`  | Sync features (the V3 pipeline, Ask LEO, escalation, etc.)   | Sync   |
| `libs.llm_client.providers.invoke_with_fallback`         | Async features that want Bedrock primary + Azure fallback    | Async  |

All three forward input / output / cache token counts, latency, and
the model id to the registered tracking callback on success and on
failure. Both `LLMClient.converse` and `invoke_with_fallback` accept
optional `agent_task` and `patient_id` kwargs that flow into the
callback verbatim.

```python
# GOOD -- async JSON helper
from libs.llm_client.json_helper import invoke_llm_json
result = await invoke_llm_json(
    system_prompt=SYS,
    user_message=usr,
    agent_task="my_feature_stage_1",
    patient_id=patient_id,
)
```

```python
# GOOD -- sync converse helper (Bedrock or Azure)
from libs.llm_client.factory import create_llm
client = create_llm(provider="aws", tier="big")
response = client.converse(
    system=SYS,
    messages=[{"role": "user", "content": usr}],
    agent_task="ask_leo_smart",
    patient_id=patient_id,
)
```

```python
# GOOD -- async Bedrock-with-Azure-fallback helper
from libs.llm_client.providers import get_bedrock_model, invoke_with_fallback
model = await get_bedrock_model()
response = await invoke_with_fallback(
    model,
    messages=messages,
    agent_task="pipeline_fix_analyzer",
    patient_id=patient_id,
)
```

```python
# BAD -- bypasses token extraction; cost will silently disappear
from langchain_aws import ChatBedrockConverse
model = ChatBedrockConverse(...)
response = await model.ainvoke(messages)  # no telemetry path
```

If you absolutely must call a provider client directly (rare -- e.g.
streaming, tool use, embeddings), you MUST replicate the work the
sanctioned helpers do: time the call with `time.monotonic`, extract
usage via `libs.llm_client.token_tracker.extract_token_counts`, and
call `track_llm_usage(...)` (or `track_llm_usage_sync(...)` from a
sync context) with `model_name`, `model_provider`, `agent_task`,
`patient_id`, `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`,
`cache_read_input_tokens`, `cache_creation_input_tokens`,
`latency_ms`, `success`, `error_message`. Fire on the failure path
too, so cost-monitoring sees outages.

## 2. Orchestrators MUST Wrap a Logical Run in `LLMUsageRecorder`

Anything that issues more than one LLM call as part of a single
logical run (a pipeline job, an SBAR generation, an episode-engine
run, a batch coder) MUST scope the work in `LLMUsageRecorder` so the
totals can be persisted.

```python
# GOOD
from libs.llm_client.usage_recorder import LLMUsageRecorder
from libs.llm_usage import LLMCostConfig

with LLMUsageRecorder() as rec:
    await invoke_llm_json(...)   # stage 1
    await invoke_llm_json(...)   # stage 2

cfg = LLMCostConfig.from_env()
self._record_telemetry(recorder=rec, ...)  # see rule 3
```

The recorder uses `contextvars.ContextVar`, so concurrent asyncio
tasks each get an isolated copy. Do NOT introduce a module-global or
threading.local accumulator.

## 3. On Finalise, Persist Two Surfaces

To make the run visible to the dashboard `LLMSpendPanel`, the
per-tenant billing endpoint `/pricing/orgs`, the Mission Control
`AuditTrailTab`, and the per-patient drill-down
`/analytics/llm-spend/patient`, the orchestrator MUST write BOTH:

### 3.1 Entity-level `llm_usage_json` + flat fields

Match the established `:EncounterCandidate` pattern. For SBAR this is
done by `libs/cypher/sbar_assessment_queries.py::SET_ASSESSMENT_USAGE`
on the `:Assessment` node. For new entities, mirror that schema:

| Field                   | Type   | Source                                      |
|-------------------------|--------|---------------------------------------------|
| `llm_usage_json`        | string | `json.dumps(rec.to_audit_dict(cfg))`        |
| `llm_input_tokens`      | int    | `rec.usage.input_tokens`                    |
| `llm_output_tokens`     | int    | `rec.usage.output_tokens`                   |
| `llm_cached_tokens`     | int    | `rec.usage.cached_input_tokens`             |
| `llm_total_tokens`      | int    | `rec.usage.total_tokens`                    |
| `llm_calls`             | int    | `rec.usage.llm_calls`                       |
| `llm_cost_usd`          | float  | `round(rec.cost_usd(cfg), 6)`               |
| `llm_latency_ms`        | int    | `rec.total_latency_ms`                      |
| `llm_model_id`          | string | `rec.primary_model`                         |
| `llm_model_provider`    | string | `rec.primary_provider`                      |

Then extend `libs/cypher/model_config_queries.py::GET_PATIENT_LLM_SPEND`
with a UNION over the new entity (use a `source` discriminator string,
e.g. `'sbar_assessment'`, `'episode_engine_run'`).

### 3.2 A `:AuditEvent {type:'PipelineRun'}` linked to the patient

This is the surface read by `LLMSpendPanel` (via
`/analytics/llm-spend/runs`) and per-tenant billing. Use the same
flat field names as `libs/workflow/engine.py::_write_audit_event`:

```cypher
MERGE (ae:AuditEvent {id: $id})
SET ae.type                   = 'PipelineRun',
    ae.patient_id             = $patient_id,
    ae.encounter_id           = $encounter_id,
    ae.run_id                 = $run_id,
    ae.event_type             = $event_type,
    ae.status                 = $status,
    ae.step_count             = $step_count,
    ae.total_duration_ms      = $total_duration_ms,
    ae.entity_count           = $entity_count,
    ae.error_count            = $error_count,
    ae.first_error            = $first_error,
    ae.llm_input_tokens       = $llm_input_tokens,
    ae.llm_output_tokens      = $llm_output_tokens,
    ae.llm_cached_tokens      = $llm_cached_tokens,
    ae.llm_cost_usd           = $llm_cost_usd,
    ae.extraction_provider    = $extraction_provider,
    ae.extraction_model_tier  = $extraction_model_tier,
    ae.extraction_prompt_name = $extraction_prompt_name,
    ae.extraction_prompt_version = $extraction_prompt_version,
    ae.created_at             = datetime()
WITH ae
OPTIONAL MATCH (p:Patient {id: $patient_id})
FOREACH (_ IN CASE WHEN p IS NOT NULL THEN [1] ELSE [] END |
    MERGE (ae)-[:AUDIT_FOR]->(p)
)
```

Reuse `WRITE_SBAR_AUDIT_EVENT` as the canonical template.

## 4. Telemetry Writes MUST Be Best-Effort

A failure to record telemetry MUST NEVER fail the underlying run.
Wrap every Cypher write for telemetry in its own try / except and log
at WARNING:

```python
# GOOD
try:
    session.run(SET_ASSESSMENT_USAGE, ...)
except Exception:
    logger.warning(
        "telemetry: failed to set llm_usage_json for %s",
        assessment_id, exc_info=True,
    )

try:
    session.run(WRITE_SBAR_AUDIT_EVENT, ...)
except Exception:
    logger.warning(
        "telemetry: failed to write PipelineRun AuditEvent for %s",
        run_id, exc_info=True,
    )
```

```python
# BAD -- a Neo4j blip will fail the whole job
session.run(SET_ASSESSMENT_USAGE, ...)
session.run(WRITE_SBAR_AUDIT_EVENT, ...)
```

## 5. Numeric Discipline

- All token counts MUST be `int(...)` (not float, not None).
- All cost amounts MUST be `round(value, 6)` before writing to Neo4j
  to avoid float drift in aggregations.
- Negative values are forbidden -- clamp with `max(0, ...)` if a
  provider response could ever produce one.

## 6. Checklist Before Merging Any New LLM Call Site

- [ ] All LLM calls go through one of the three sanctioned entry
      points -- `invoke_llm_json`, `LLMClient.converse`, or
      `invoke_with_fallback` -- OR replicate their
      `extract_token_counts` + `track_llm_usage(_sync)` plumbing.
- [ ] When calling `LLMClient.converse` or `invoke_with_fallback`,
      `agent_task` and `patient_id` are passed (default
      `"unknown"` / `""` is only acceptable for the genuinely
      patientless infra paths).
- [ ] Logical run wrapped in `with LLMUsageRecorder() as rec:`.
- [ ] Entity node carries `llm_usage_json` + the 9 flat fields from
      table 3.1.
- [ ] A `:AuditEvent {type:'PipelineRun'}` is MERGEd with
      `[:AUDIT_FOR]->(:Patient)` and the same flat fields.
- [ ] Both telemetry writes are inside their own try / except with a
      WARNING log on failure.
- [ ] If a new persistent surface was introduced (e.g. a new entity
      label that carries `llm_usage_json`), `GET_PATIENT_LLM_SPEND`
      has been extended with a UNION over it and a `source`
      discriminator.
- [ ] Pytest cases assert: token counts on the recorder, the entity
      `llm_usage_json` write, the AuditEvent write, and that a
      simulated telemetry failure does NOT fail the run.

## 7. Where the Wire Format Is Consumed

Do not change the field names or shapes without first updating every
consumer below:

| Consumer                                                   | Reads from                                              |
|------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|
| `services/ui/src/components/dashboard/LLMSpendPanel.tsx`   | `GET /api/analytics/llm-spend/runs`                     |
| `services/ui/src/components/mission-control/AuditTrailTab` | `:AuditEvent` properties directly via Mission Control   |
| `GET /api/analytics/llm-spend/patient`                     | `GET_PATIENT_LLM_SPEND` -> `llm_usage_json`             |
| `GET /api/pricing/orgs` (per-tenant billing)               | `:AuditEvent {type:'PipelineRun'}` flat `llm_*` fields  |
| `services/ui/src/lib/types.ts::LLMUsage`                   | `LLMUsage.to_dict(cost_config)` Python output           |
